<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  ProductivityDashboard sandbox entitlements.

  Minimum-necessary principle (CLAUDE.md, Security & Privacy):
  this file lists ONLY the OS capabilities the app strictly requires.
  Before adding any key here, justify it against the privacy boundary
  in CLAUDE.md ("no telemetry / no extra network calls", "the allowlist
  gate is the spine"). Sandbox entitlements expand the app's reach
  beyond what TCC prompts cover at runtime — keep this list small and
  deliberate.

  Current keys:

  - com.apple.security.app-sandbox
      Declares the app sandbox. Listed explicitly (rather than relying
      on the ENABLE_APP_SANDBOX build setting alone) so this file is
      self-contained and the sandbox state is obvious from reading
      entitlements directly.

  - com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars
      Required for EventKit reads. Without this, EKEventStore calls
      fail silently before reaching TCC, so the macOS permission
      prompt never appears (this bit us once during Stage 2 setup).
      Read-only intent is enforced in code — EventKit has no
      read-only entitlement variant; see EventKitCalendarSource.swift.

  - com.apple.security.network.client
      Required for outgoing TCP to mail and API servers used by the app:
        * Stage 3: imap.gmail.com:993 (IMAPS, fetch user's inbox)
        * Stage 5: api.anthropic.com:443 (HTTPS, Claude API for analysis
          of allowlisted mail only — the allowlist gate is enforced in
          code; see CLAUDE.md Security & Privacy items 1–2)
      The sandbox does not provide a host-scoped variant; this is a
      single boolean for "may initiate outbound connections at all".

  Never add — explicit constraint, do not relax without re-reading
  CLAUDE.md Security & Privacy:

  - com.apple.security.network.server
      The app never listens for inbound connections. There is no
      feature in CLAUDE.md (current or roadmapped) that requires this.
      If you find yourself wanting it, stop and reconsider — it almost
      certainly indicates a design drift away from the privacy posture.
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
